  "output_text": "**Context:**  \ncircRMST knockdown in SHP77 cells (NEPC/SCLC model) caused 70–93% depletion, leading to cell cycle arrest and suppressed tumor growth. RNA-seq identified differentially expressed genes (DEGs) post-knockdown.  \n\n**Keywords:**  \ncircRMST, neuroendocrine prostate cancer (NEPC), small cell lung cancer (SCLC), cell cycle arrest, RNA-seq, differentially expressed genes (DEGs), GSEA, therapeutic target.  \n\n**Candidate Genes:**  \nASCL1, CD24, RAB3B, PTP4A1, ITGB1, SESN3, STC1, DHRS2.  \n\n**Pathway Enrichments:**  \n*Analysis based on DEG directionality (shRNA1/shRNA2 combined):*  \n- **Upregulated pathways:**  \n  - Cell adhesion (ITGB1, CD24);  \n  - Stress response (SESN3, STC1);  \n  - Metabolism (FTH1, PGM2L1).  \n- **Downregulated pathways:**  \n  - Cell cycle progression (ASCL1, DHRS2, EIF3I);  \n  - Neuroendocrine differentiation (ASCL1, GRP);  \n  - Ribosome biogenesis (RPL genes).  \n\n**Targeted Subset:**  \nASCL1 (downregulated, log2FC -3.07) is a master transcription factor in NEPC, directly linked to neuroendocrine identity and tumor growth.  \n\n**Key Genes/Proteins (Leading Edge):**  \n**Upregulated:**  \n| Gene    | Direction | Role/Function                | Pathway(s)              |  \n|---------|-----------|------------------------------|-------------------------|  \n| ITGB1   | Up        | Cell adhesion, migration     | Focal adhesion          |  \n| SESN3   | Up        | Stress response, DNA repair  | p53 signaling           |  \n\n**Downregulated:**  \n| Gene    | Direction | Role/Function                | Pathway(s)              |  \n|---------|-----------|------------------------------|-------------------------|  \n| ASCL1   | Down      | Neuroendocrine specification | Notch signaling         |  \n| DHRS2   | Down      | Retinol metabolism           | Cell cycle regulation   |  \n\n**Implications:**  \nASCL1 downregulation aligns with impaired neuroendocrine identity and tumor growth. Downregulation of ribosomal genes (EIF3I) suggests translational suppression.  \n\n**Next Steps:**  \n1. Validate ASCL1 as a direct circRMST target using RNA pulldown assays.  \n2. Assess rescue of ASCL1 expression in circRMST-knockdown models to confirm phenotypic reversal.  \n3. Perform GSEA using the ranked DEG list to confirm pathway enrichments.  \n\n**References:**  \nASCL1's role in NEPC validated in PMID 31537894 and 29374185.",
